/**
 * @defgroup module_ui User Interface
 * @ingroup module_core
 * @brief Terminal presentation, input routing, widgets, and interactive screens.
 */

/**
 * @page topic_ui User Interface Architecture
 * @ingroup module_ui
 * @brief How ascii-chat presents live state and routes interaction.
 *
 * The UI is split into reusable widgets, the TUI screen/controller layer, and
 * the platform keyboard decoder. Producers publish snapshots; they do not
 * write directly to the terminal or own keyboard policy.
 *
 * @section ui_boundaries Boundaries
 *
 * - `lib/ui/` and `include/ascii-chat/ui/` contain reusable widgets.
 * - `lib/tui/` and `include/ascii-chat/tui/` contain complete screens, snapshots,
 *   input routing, and the controller.
 * - `lib/platform/keyboard.c` normalizes POSIX escape sequences, Windows console
 *   events, UTF-8, and UTF-16 into `keyboard_key_t`.
 * - `lib/platform/terminal.c` owns terminal geometry, capabilities, raw mode,
 *   and restoration.
 *
 * @section ui_controller Controller and screens
 *
 * `ui_controller_submit()` copies a screen snapshot and selects the highest
 * priority live screen. Covered screens remain registered, so dismissing a
 * prompt or help overlay restores the previous owner. Rendering callbacks run
 * without the controller mutex; producers must not hold a lock required by a
 * callback while removing its screen.
 *
 * The controller owns the output sink. Live screen output goes through
 * `ui_controller_write()` or `ui_controller_present()` so logs, prompts, and
 * media cannot paint over one another. `ui_controller_finish()` retires live
 * screens before synchronous final output.
 *
 * @section ui_screens Screen model
 *
 * The runtime includes status, media, splash, progress, logs, error stacks,
 * help, statistics, sync diagnostics, mDNS selection, update, notice, prompt,
 * and error screens. Screens declare a minimum terminal size. When the terminal
 * is too small, `tui/too_small.h` is presented and the underlying screen is
 * restored after resize.
 *
 * @section ui_input Input routing
 *
 * `lib/tui/input.c` reads decoded events and routes them according to the
 * active screen. Modal prompts consume editing keys; covered screens do not
 * receive shortcuts. Bracketed paste is validated as a complete event and is
 * never interpreted as a sequence of application shortcuts. See
 * @ref topic_keyboard_shortcuts for the current bindings.
 *
 * @section ui_threading Threading and shutdown
 *
 * Producers may publish snapshots from worker threads. The controller copies
 * owned snapshot data and callbacks execute on the presentation thread. Shutdown
 * stops producers, retires screens, joins presentation, restores the terminal,
 * then tears down keyboard and logging state.
 *
 * @see topic_tui
 * @see topic_keyboard_shortcuts
 * @see md_docs_2terminal-ui.html
 */
